### Snippet 3 - Using the `WebsiteManager` class in a console application

This example demonstrates how to use the `WebsiteManager` class in a console application. The code creates an instance of the `WebsiteManager` class and uses it to manage websites on the local machine.

```csharp
using System;
using WebsiteManagerLib;

namespace WebsiteManagerConsoleApp
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            // Create a new instance of the WebsiteManager class
            var websiteManager = new WebsiteManager();

            try
            {
                // Add a new website to the local machine
                websiteManager.AddWebsite("Test Website", @"C:\inetpub\testwebsite");
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                Console.WriteLine($"Error adding website: {ex.Message}");
            }

            try
            {
                // Update the metadata of an existing website
                websiteManager.UpdateWebsite("Test Website", @"C:\inetpub\testwebsite2");
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                Console.WriteLine($"Error updating website: {ex.Message}");
            }

            try
            {
                // Remove an existing website from the local machine
                websiteManager.RemoveWebsite("Test Website");
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                Console.WriteLine($"Error removing website: {ex.Message}");
            }
        }
    }
}
```

