To account for potential performance bottlenecks during high-frequency logging events, the function uses a buffering mechanism that stores messages until the logging service is available. This helps to avoid overloading the logging service with too many requests at once, which can lead to performance issues. The buffering mechanism also allows the function to intelligently determine when it should submit logs and when it should buffer them.

To design the function to scale effectively under heavy load, the function uses a thread-safe lock to protect access to the logging service. This helps to ensure that the function can handle high levels of traffic without interfering with other components of the system. The function also includes mechanisms for retrying failed log submissions and intelligently buffering messages when the logging service is unavailable, which help to minimize performance bottlenecks.

