The `add_packet_header` function adds a new packet header to the list by first checking if the list is full. If it is not full, the function allocates memory for the new packet header and copies the given source and destination IP addresses, port numbers, protocol identifier, and unique identifier into it. The function then increments the `size` member of the list to keep track of the number of packets in the list.

