The `filter_packet_headers` function filters packet headers based on IP addresses or protocols. It starts by checking if any of the given IP addresses, source and destination, are non-zero. If they are, the function iterates through all the packet headers in the list and removes any header that matches one of the specified IP addresses or protocols using `remove_packet_header`.

Finally, the `destroy_packet_list` function frees the memory allocated by the packet list using `free`. The function also logs an error message if any errors occur during deallocation.

