This implementation of the logging system uses a `Logger` class to handle the actual logging, and provides several `LoggingBackend` classes that can be used to store the logged events. The `FileLoggingBackend` stores the events in a file on disk, while the `InMemoryLoggingBackend` stores them in memory.

The `Logger` class is responsible for handling all the logging tasks, such as formatting the log messages and storing them in the appropriate backend. It also provides methods for retrieving logged events and for clearing the stored events.

The `FileLoggingBackend` class uses the standard C++ file I/O library to handle the actual file operations. It opens the log file for writing when it is created, and closes it when it is destroyed. When adding a new event to the backend, it writes the event to the file using the `std::ofstream` object. When removing an event from the backend, it removes the corresponding line from the file.

The `InMemoryLoggingBackend` class stores the events in memory using a `std::map` data structure. When adding a new event to the backend, it adds it to the map and returns the identifier of the added event. When removing an event from the backend, it removes the corresponding entry from the map.

To use the logging system, you can create a `Logger` object and specify the desired logging level and the backend where the events should be stored. For example:
```cpp
int main() {
    Logger logger("MyLogger", Logger::INFO);
    FileLoggingBackend fileBackend("logs/mylog.txt");
    logger.addBackend(&fileBackend);
    logger.info("This is an info message.");
    logger.debug("This is a debug message.");
}
```
In this example, the `Logger` object is created with the name "MyLogger" and the logging level set to `INFO`. The `FileLoggingBackend` object is created with the name "logs/mylog.txt", which will store all logged events in a file named "mylog.txt". The `Logger` object is then added as a backend to the `fileBackend`, and the `logger.info()` method is used to log an info message, while the `logger.debug()` method is used to log a debug message.']

