```c
// Function to add a packet to the monitoring tool
void monitor_packet(struct PacketBuffer *buffer, const char *packet, size_t length) {
    // Lock the buffer to prevent concurrent access
    pthread_mutex_lock(&buffer_lock);

    // Parse the incoming packet using the third-party library
    struct packet_metadata metadata;
    int ret = packet_parse(packet, length, &metadata);
    if (ret == 0) {
        // Add the parsed metadata to the monitoring tool's data structures
        monitoring_tool_add_packet(buffer->count, metadata.id, metadata.timestamp, metadata.src_ip, metadata.dest_ip, metadata.protocol);
    } else {
        perror("Failed to parse incoming packet");
    }

    // Unlock the buffer and return
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&buffer_lock);
}
```
In summary, this function uses a mutex lock to protect the buffer from concurrent access, dynamic resizing of the buffer to balance memory usage against the need for rapid resizing, robust error handling to manage failures gracefully and provide informative error messages. It is designed to be compatible with an existing packet processing framework and maintain compatibility with existing logging and monitoring systems.']

