This implementation uses a mutex to synchronize access to the array and a condition variable to signal when the resize threshold is reached. The function also checks for memory allocation failures and exits with an error message if any occur. Additionally, the function initializes all elements of the array to zero before returning.

The performance implications of this implementation are dependent on the specific requirements of the production environment. However, using a mutex and condition variable can help to minimize contention and maximize throughput by ensuring that only one thread at a time can access the array. Additionally, resizing the array dynamically can help to improve the efficiency of the function by avoiding unnecessary memory allocation and deallocation.

